SUMMARY:Family Day
DESCRIPTION:Family Day            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Sundays\n11:00 am – 3:00 pm\nMakerspace\, Ground Floor\nFree for kids and included with admission for adults and seniors. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Families can connect over clay in our new Makerspace with weekly activities inspired by our collection and special exhibitions\, and led by our amazing team of educators and volunteers. In celebration of National Indigenous Peoples Day\, we invite you to get inspired by the Indigenous ceramics in our galleries and create your own miniature vessels and pinch pot animals. Gather the whole family and get creative with clay! \nWe recommend bringing a recycled container or bag in which to transport your work home. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/family-day-june-24-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Family Days,Programs & Events
